{"archetypes":[{"name":"token-enum-sync","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Retired cancelled-tier-gate and --simple must be consistently absent from every enum surface; the diff touches the main ones but .claude-plugin/plugin.json (named in the plan) is absent from the diff entirely and could still carry stale references.","prompt_body":"Verify that the `cancelled-tier-gate` outcome token has been retired from every enum surface listed in the plan: `skills/design/SKILL.md` orchestrator-contract enum, `render-final-summary.sh` case branch, `render-final-summary.md` Callers section, `test-render-final-summary.sh` all-outcomes loop, and `scripts/render-run-summary.md` outcomes table. Also verify that `--simple` (the retired argv token) is absent from all live-surface files — specifically `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, which the plan names as a required change but which does not appear anywhere in the diff. Cross-check that the `SUMMARY_OUTCOME` enum in SKILL.md matches the `case` allowlist in `render-final-summary.sh` exactly, with no token present in one but missing from the other. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"flag-rejection-impl","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds prose to SKILL.md saying any disallowed leading public -- flag is a hard error before Step 0, but no shell implementation of that rejection gate appears anywhere in the diff; the gate could be documentation-only with no runtime enforcement.","prompt_body":"The diff adds to `skills/design/SKILL.md` the rule that any unrecognized or disallowed leading public `--` flag is a hard error before Step 0 and is never treated as positional feature text. Check whether this rejection is actually enforced in a shell script (e.g., the flag-parsing portion of the design bootstrap or `scripts/session-setup.sh`) or whether it exists only as SKILL.md prose that the orchestrator is expected to follow. If a script implements flag parsing, verify that the allowlist matches the post-change public flag set (`--hard`, `-p`, `--partition`, `--brainstorm`, `--manual`, `-m`, `--no-dedup`, `--run-id`) and that unknown flags exit non-zero before any `DESIGN_TMPDIR` is created. Also check whether the `test-design-structure.sh` new assertion needle `'unrecognized or disallowed leading public \`--\` flag is a hard error before Step 0'` is an accurate substring of the actual SKILL.md prose added (verbatim match matters for shell `grep -Fq`). Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
